<title>CHINA: Housing and Commercial Bank mandates FRN.</title>
<headline>Housing and Commercial Bank mandates FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Housing and Commercial Bank has mandated four banks to arrange a US$150 million floating-rate notes issue, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said the notes would carry a maturity of three years and have put and call options on the first and second anniversary.</p>
<p>Pricing details were not available.</p>
<p>LTCB Asia, ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, Fuji International Finance (HK) and Merrill Lynch are arrangers.</p>
<p>Housing and Commercial Bank, a state-backed housing loan provider, is rated A1 by Moody's Investors Service.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
